course: dictionary
lesson: 12135
title: Committed: one word, several meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one is meant. The word committed is a good example. Read the words around it and ask which meaning fits best.
explain: «Maya is committed to her football team and never misses training.» Here committed means loyal and hardworking. Now read «The thief committed the crime at night.» Here committed is the past form of commit, and it means did something wrong.
explain: Check your choice by swapping in your meaning. If committed means promised, does «She committed to helping her sister» still make sense? Yes, so that meaning fits.
fact: «Committed» can describe a person who works hard at something and stays loyal to it.
fact: Committed is also the past form of commit, so «He committed a foul» means he did something wrong in a game.
fact: «Committed to» means promised or agreed to do something, as in «committed to finishing the project».
fact: In formal news, «committed» can mean officially sent to prison, hospital or trial.
fact: Phrases to know: committed to, committed a crime, committed a foul, fully committed.
exercise: «Ben is committed to his guitar lessons and practises every day.» What does committed mean here? | *Loyal and hardworking | Very cold | Sent to prison | Did something wrong
exercise: «The man committed a crime and was caught by the police.» What does committed mean here? | Promised to help | *Did something wrong | Felt sad | Worked very hard
exercise: Which phrase means someone is loyal to something and gives it all their effort? | *fully committed | committed a foul | committed a crime
test: «The footballer committed a foul in the penalty box.» What does committed mean here? | Sent away | Promised | Trained hard | *Did something wrong
test: «Sam committed to the trip and bought his ticket.» What does committed to mean here? | *Promised to go | Did a crime | Forgot all about it | Got lost
exam: «The charity committed the money to building a new school.» What does committed mean here? | Lost in the post | Stolen | Forgotten | *Set aside for a project
